From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bgfx: load GL entry points through EGL when there is no libGL

On Linux, bgfx's GL backend takes its entry points from libGL.so.1. A
Mesa built for EGL only (no GLX) has no libGL, but EGL 1.5's
eglGetProcAddress returns every GL function, core ones included, so
fall back to it.

Upstream: not sent
Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/theseus/third-party/bgfx/src/glcontext_egl.cpp b/theseus/third-party/bgfx/src/glcontext_egl.cpp
index c722b45..48cb01e 100644
--- a/theseus/third-party/bgfx/src/glcontext_egl.cpp
+++ b/theseus/third-party/bgfx/src/glcontext_egl.cpp
@@ -800,11 +800,17 @@ WL_EGL_IMPORT
 
 		void* lib = bx::dlopen(LIBRARY_NAME);
 
+		// A Mesa without GLX ships no libGL.so.1, but EGL 1.5 hands out every
+		// GL entry point (core ones included) through eglGetProcAddress.
 #		define GL_EXTENSION(_optional, _proto, _func, _import)                           \
 			{                                                                            \
 				if (NULL == _func)                                                       \
 				{                                                                        \
-					_func = bx::dlsym<_proto>(lib, #_import);                            \
+					_func = NULL != lib ? bx::dlsym<_proto>(lib, #_import) : NULL;       \
+					if (NULL == _func)                                                   \
+					{                                                                    \
+						_func = reinterpret_cast<_proto>(eglGetProcAddress(#_import) );  \
+					}                                                                    \
 					BX_TRACE("\t%p " #_func " (" #_import ")", _func);                   \
 					BGFX_FATAL(_optional || NULL != _func                                \
 						, Fatal::UnableToInitialize                                      \
